## DeprecatedGraphQLFieldInline

**Severity:** warning | **Type:** LiquidHtml

This check is the inline half of [DeprecatedGraphQLField](/developer-guide/platformos-check/checks/deprecated-graphql-field). It reports a schema member marked `@deprecated` used inside an inline `{% raw %}{% graphql %}…{% endgraphql %}{% endraw %}` block.

Two checks rather than one, because severity is a property of the check and these are not the same severity. An invalid query fails when it executes; a deprecated query runs and returns data. Reporting both under one code would make every deprecation an error, or every invalid inline query a warning.

Inline bodies use deprecated members at more than twice the rate of `.graphql` documents, so this is where most of the deprecated surface in a real application is.

The message is the schema's own `@deprecated(reason:)` text, and the offense is reported on the deprecated name inside the `.liquid` file. The check requires an up-to-date local copy of the platformOS GraphQL schema. Run `pos-cli check update-docs` to download the latest schema.

## Examples

### &#x2717; Incorrect Code Example (Avoid using this):

```liquid
{% raw %}
{% graphql result %}
  query {
    models(per_page: 20, filter: { name: { value: "note" } }) {
      results { id }
    }
  }
{% endgraphql %}
{% endraw %}
```

`RootQuery.models` is deprecated. The page renders and returns data; nothing fails.

### &#x2713; Correct Code Example (Use this instead):

```liquid
{% raw %}
{% graphql result %}
  query {
    records(per_page: 20, filter: { table: { value: "note" } }) {
      results { id }
    }
  }
{% endgraphql %}
{% endraw %}
```

## What is not reported

The same two exclusions as [GraphQLInlineCheck](/developer-guide/platformos-check/checks/graphql-inline-check): a body that interpolates Liquid is not validated, and a body that does not parse is left alone.

## Configuration

The default configuration for this check:

```yaml
DeprecatedGraphQLFieldInline:
  enabled: true
  severity: warning
```

## Disabling This Check

This check is safe to disable while you are maintaining code against an older platform version, or during a migration where the deprecated form is still deliberate.

```yaml
DeprecatedGraphQLFieldInline:
  enabled: false
```

